{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Keel washing machine and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You asked if you should run another cycle to see if the burning smell clears. Our help article "Burning smell from your Keel washing machine" says you must stop using the machine immediately and do not run another cycle to see if the smell clears. Please switch off and unplug the appliance, provided it is safe to do so, and contact Halvard Home support to arrange an inspection.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked whether you should dismantle your Fenwick cooker hood yourself to address an E-6292 error code before recycling the unit. Our help article "Recycling your Fenwick cooker hood" says that you must not dismantle the motor yourself. Instead, you should switch off the electricity supply and have a qualified electrician assess the fault first.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking if it is alright to plug your Ashby tumble dryer into an extension lead to avoid an electrical hazard. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. Our help article "Installing your Ashby tumble dryer" says you must not use an extension lead. You should plug your dryer directly into a suitable earthed wall socket.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the E-9509 error code displayed on your Tessa dishwasher and why your delay countdown has stopped. Our help article "Tessa dishwasher: delay start fault" says that this error means your dishwasher has lost the saved countdown for the delay start. To reset it, hold the Start button for three seconds to cancel, switch the unit off at the wall for one minute, then restart the programme and delay timer.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Ashby dryer and unplug it if it is safe to do so. I'm sorry, I can't find that in our policies. I've passed your question to a colleague who will reply within two working days.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking for the safety steps to follow regarding your Brio kettle before calling for an engineer. Our help article "Booking an engineer for your Brio kettle" says you must switch off and unplug the kettle before checking it for visible damage. Do not remove the casing or attempt internal repairs. You must stop using the appliance if it leaks, sparks or has a damaged lead.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the maintenance requirements for your Corra induction hob regarding cleaning the air vents and scheduling professional safety checks. Our Safety and recalls policy, section "Corra induction hob: Safe use", says you should clean the air vents every 16 days and have the hob safety-checked by a qualified professional every 6 months. We hope this information helps you maintain your appliance.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked if living in an M postcode area guarantees an engineer visit and what the standard call-out fee is. Our Servicing and engineer visits policy, section "North of England: Engineers in this region", says that living in a listed postcode does not automatically guarantee a visit, as coverage depends on location, access and engineer availability. The policy also states that an engineer call-out in the North of England costs £26.00.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the water dripping from the bottom of your Lumen thermostat and what steps to take first. Our help article "Water leaking underneath your Lumen thermostat" says you should not touch the thermostat while it is wet. If the switch and surrounding area are dry, switch off the heating controls at their electrical isolator and contact Halvard Home support or a qualified heating engineer.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You are asking if you should chip ice away or pour boiling water on your Orrin heat pump. Our help article "Frost or condensation on your Orrin heat pump" says you must not chip away ice or pour boiling water over the unit. If thick ice remains or returns, you should leave the unit switched off and contact Halvard Home support to arrange inspection and cleaning of the KX-9512 condensate drain insert.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You are worried about the smell of burning coming from your Lumen thermostat and asked if you should turn the temperature down. Our help article "Burning smell from your Lumen smart thermostat" says turning the temperature down does not disconnect the electrical supply. You must stop using the device and switch off the power to your heating system at the mains isolator, provided it is safe to do so.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about the time required to cool your Brio kettle after you noticed a burning smell. Our help article "Burning smell from your Brio kettle" says you must leave the kettle to cool for at least 30 minutes before checking it for damage.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking if missing accessories will affect the refund amount for your Tessa dishwasher return. Our Returns and refunds policy, section "Tessa dishwasher: Packaging and condition", says that if you return your Tessa dishwasher missing any accessories, you will receive a refund of 58% of the price.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking if you may remove the casing of your Orrin heat pump to address an E-6763 code yourself. Our help article "Orrin heat pump: first installation warning" says you must not remove the casing, loosen pipe connections, or repeatedly restart the unit. This code indicates trapped air. It is an installer task that requires them to purge the heating circuit and check the isolation valves. Please contact your installer to carry out this necessary work on your heating system as described in our instructions.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Regarding your concern that the casing of your Lumen thermostat appears to be cracked and will not stay shut, please note that you should not use tape or glue to hold the lid shut. Our help article "Lumen thermostat lid will not close" says that if the casing looks cracked, you should leave it alone and contact Halvard Home support. We have noted that you were considering using tape to secure the lid and this is not recommended according to our guidelines.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking what you should do before switching your Brio kettle back on when it shows an error message. Our help article "Brio kettle: fault message on the display" says you must stop using the kettle, switch it off at the socket, and unplug it. Leave it to cool for 15 minutes. Then ensure the water level is between the minimum and maximum marks and that the base and connections are dry. 

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the system and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have noticed a burning smell coming from your Orrin heat pump and asked if you should remove debris around the unit. Our help article "Flashing warning light on your Orrin heat pump" says that if you notice a burning smell, you must stop using the system and seek professional help promptly. Please follow this guidance regarding the burning smell you have noticed coming from your Orrin heat pump.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You are asking whether you are allowed to take off the electrical covers of your Fenwick hood to inspect a leak. Our help article "Water leaking underneath your Fenwick cooker hood" says that you must not remove electrical covers or attempt internal repairs. You must not remove these covers or attempt to repair the hood yourself.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Keel washing machine and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked what to do about the smoke coming from your machine. Our help article "Burning smell from your Keel washing machine" says that you should leave the property and call 999. It also states that you should never use water on an electrical fire.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Regarding your safety concern about your dishwasher, you asked how quickly you should expect an engineer to visit. Our Safety and recalls policy, section "Extended Care Plus: Safety checks under the plan", says as an Extended Care Plus member, you will get an engineer within 42 hours once you report the safety concern to our customer care team. This timeframe applies to your inquiry about an engineer visit for your dishwasher safety concern.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked whether you should force your latch to get the lid to click shut after checking for obstructions. Our help article "Orrin heat pump door or lid not closing" says that you should not force the latch. If it still will not close, you should leave the unit off and contact Halvard Home support.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the controls and unplug the appliance if it is safe to do so. You have asked what to do if moisture appears inside the display of your Lumen thermostat or if the controls stop responding. Our help article "Frost or condensation on your Lumen thermostat" says that if moisture appears inside the display or the controls stop responding, you must stop using the controls and contact Halvard Home support for advice.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You are asking if the E-9474 error code on your Tessa dishwasher means the heater has overheated. Our help article "Burning smell from your Tessa dishwasher" says that the E-9474 error code on the Tessa dishwasher indicates that the heater’s electrical connection has overheated. We have noted your report regarding this error code and the associated smell from your dishwasher.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking how long you should wait when your Lumen thermostat firmware update is stuck at 50% before restarting your router. Our help article "Updating your Lumen thermostat" says that if the progress has not changed for 10 minutes, you should restart your router and then tap Retry in the app. This guidance addresses your question regarding the update process for your device. 

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Corra hob and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked if you should wait for the hob to cool down before switching it off at the mains because it smells of burning plastic. Our help article "Burning smell from your Corra induction hob" says that if the smell resembles burning plastic or electrics, you should switch off the hob at the mains immediately if it is safe to do so.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You are asking how long to wait for your Fenwick cooker hood to cool before checking the filters after hearing a rattling noise. Our help article "# Fenwick cooker hood: strange noise during use" says you should wait ten minutes for the cooker hood to cool before checking the filters.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your cooker and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about the waiting time for an urgent safety visit in Birmingham. Our Safety and recalls policy, section "Midlands: Safety visits in this region", says urgent safety visits in the Midlands are made within 32 hours. This provides the timeframe for when a visit is conducted following an urgent safety report in your specific region.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and ensure it remains unplugged. Regarding your question about how long you must wait for your Brio kettle to cool down after smelling burning plastic, our help article "Burning smell from your Brio kettle" says you must leave the kettle to cool for at least 30 minutes before checking it for damage.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking how long to wait after closing the app before attempting to add your Vale fridge again. Our help article "Vale fridge freezer not found in the app" says you should wait 10 seconds before reopening the app and attempting to add the appliance again.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Keel machine and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You asked if you should run a short cycle to see if the burning smell clears. Our help article "Burning smell from your Keel washing machine" says you should not run another cycle to see whether the smell clears. It says you should stop using the machine immediately and contact Halvard Home support to arrange an inspection.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your hob and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about the speed of an engineer visit for your safety concern under the Extended Care Plus plan. Our Safety and recalls policy, section "Extended Care Plus: Safety checks under the plan", says that as an Extended Care Plus member reporting a safety concern, we send an engineer to you within 42 hours. Please state to our customer care team that you are reporting a safety issue so we can arrange the appropriate response.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking about how often you should clean the air vents on your Corra induction hob to maintain it properly. Our Safety and recalls policy, section "Corra induction hob: Safe use", says you should clean the air vents every 16 days. Ensure you follow the instructions for accessing and cleaning them without removing protective covers and keep the openings free from grease, dust and obstructions. This schedule helps you maintain your appliance.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about a plasticky smell from your Tessa dishwasher and the E-9474 error code. Our help article "Burning smell from your Tessa dishwasher" says you should stop the programme and switch the dishwasher off. If it is safe to do so, disconnect the power at the wall socket or the household circuit breaker. Do not attempt to restart it or repair the wiring.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the wait time required after entering your password to connect your Orrin heat pump to wi-fi. Our help article "Connecting your Orrin heat pump to wi-fi" says you should wait one minute for the connection to complete.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked if you should leave your Orrin heat pump running while it shakes violently and moves on its base. Our help article "Unusual vibration from your Orrin heat pump" says you must keep the unit switched off if it shakes violently or moves on its base. This is the information you requested regarding the operation of your unit.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You asked if turning the temperature down on the display stops the power to your Lumen thermostat. Our help article "Burning smell from your Lumen smart thermostat" says turning the temperature down does not disconnect the electrical supply. You must switch off the power to your heating system at its mains isolator if you can reach it safely.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked how long you should wait before checking your Brio kettle for any visible damage or melted plastic after smelling burning. Our help article "Burning smell from your Brio kettle" says you should leave the kettle to cool for at least 30 minutes before checking it for any signs of damage.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked if you can cut the wires of your thermostat to remove it from the wall quickly today. Our help article "Recycling your old Lumen smart thermostat" says you must not cut wires or open the casing yourself. It says please ask a qualified electrician or heating engineer to disconnect the thermostat safely.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You asked about removing the battery from your Mira vacuum and disposing of it in your household bin. Our help article "Recycling your Mira robot vacuum" says you must not put the vacuum or battery in your household rubbish. You must leave the battery inside the unit, contact Halvard Home support to check if a replacement is suitable, and take the device to a local household waste recycling centre that accepts electrical appliances.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about the power supply steps for your Ashby tumble dryer after an E-6876 error and water leak. Our help article "Water leaking underneath your Ashby tumble dryer" says you should stop the programme and switch off the dryer. If the plug, socket and surrounding area are dry, you may unplug it, but if they are wet, you must switch off the circuit at the consumer unit instead.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the correct temperature settings for your Vale fridge and freezer while you are away with food stored inside. Our help article "Using your Vale fridge freezer in a holiday home" says that if you are keeping food inside, set the fridge to 4°C and the freezer to -18°C.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the cooling time needed before you can safely inspect the inside of your Brio kettle to check for chalky deposits. Our help article "# Brio kettle making a strange noise" says you should unplug the kettle and leave it to cool for at least 30 minutes before looking inside.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked if you should try to pull your Tessa dishwasher out to investigate the water pooling underneath it. Our help article "Water leaking under your Tessa dishwasher" says that you must not pull out the dishwasher or remove any panels to look for leaks. You are concerned about the water pooling under your appliance and the mess it is causing in your home. Please follow the instructions provided to ensure that you do not attempt to move the unit yourself at this stage.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about a continuous buzzing sound from your Lumen thermostat and how long a normal heating cycle lasts. Our help article "Lumen thermostat making a buzzing noise" says a brief click when heating starts or stops is normal. However, a continuous buzz lasting more than 10 seconds can indicate a loose coil inside the heating relay module.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked how to safely shut down your Orrin heat pump due to a burning smell. Our help article "Burning smell from your Orrin heat pump" says you must switch the unit off at the controller and then disconnect the power using the labelled isolation switch. Switching off at the controller alone does not isolate the electricity.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked if it is okay to pull your Tessa dishwasher out from under the counter to inspect a leak. Our help article "Water leaking under your Tessa dishwasher" says you must not pull out the dishwasher or remove any panels. If the source of the leak remains unclear, you should contact Halvard Home support to arrange an inspection.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Mira vacuum and unplug it if it is safe to do so. Regarding your question about taking the casing apart because of a burning smell, our help article "Burning smell from your Mira robot vacuum" says you must not dismantle the battery or open the casing. Please only remove loose material from the brush and wheels that you can reach without opening the casing, and contact Halvard Home support before using the vacuum again.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking for the safest way to remove ice buildup from your Vale fridge freezer without damaging the appliance. Our help article "Frost or condensation in your Vale fridge freezer" says you should unplug the appliance and move your food to suitable cold storage before defrosting. It also states that you must never use sharp tools or a hairdryer to remove the ice.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Fenwick cooker hood and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about cleaning grease filters when there is a burning smell. Our help article "Burning smell from your Fenwick cooker hood" says that once the hood has completely cooled, you may clean the removable grease filters according to the user guide. You must keep the hood switched off until a qualified service engineer has inspected it. You should not attempt to remove electrical covers or repair the motor.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Regarding the puddle you have spotted under your KX-3928 washing machine during its draining cycle, you should stop using the machine, switch it off, and close the water supply tap. Unplug the machine only if the plug and surrounding area are dry and safe to reach. Please ensure you do not attempt to remove panels or seal the leak yourself. Our help article "Booking a Keel engineer visit" says you should take these steps.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about the expected wait time for an engineer visit regarding a potential electrical fault with your oven. Our Safety and recalls policy, section "Extended Care: Safety checks under the plan", says that as an Extended Care member reporting a safety concern, you will have an engineer attend within 7 hours of reporting the issue to us. We understand you are concerned about the time it takes for this visit to occur. 

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked if you should continue using your Ashby tumble dryer when there is a tear in the lint filter. Our help article "Replacing a damaged lint filter" says you should stop using the dryer until the damaged filter has been replaced with the KX-3639 part, as lint can otherwise pass into the dryer's airflow system.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the steps to resolve an E-1216 error on your Fenwick hood. Our help article "Fan speed signal fault" says that to reset the hood, you should turn it off using the controls, switch off the power at the wall for five minutes, then restore the power and select the lowest fan setting. If the message clears and the fan runs normally, the unit is ready for use.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Vale fridge freezer and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about the burning smell coming from the back of your unit and if you can unscrew the back panel to perform repairs yourself. Our help article "Burning smell from your Vale fridge freezer" says the burning smell is caused by overheated contacts inside the KX-2645 compressor start relay. You must not remove covers or attempt to repair the part yourself, as you need to contact Halvard Home support to arrange an inspection by a qualified technician.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking how you know that your Brio kettle has finished the factory reset process. Our help article "Resetting your Brio kettle" says the reset is complete when the indicator light flashes twice after you have held the power button for 10 seconds. This information explains how you can identify that the reset process is finished on your appliance.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked how long you should leave your Corra hob to cool down when the E-6779 error appears. Our help article "Corra induction hob heating slowly" says that you should leave the hob to cool for 20 minutes before restoring the power.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Brio kettle and unplug it if it is safe to do so. Regarding your question about how to proceed after your Brio kettle boiled dry, our help article "Brio kettle not switching on" says you should unplug the kettle and allow it to cool fully before refilling it. This procedure addresses the situation where the kettle has boiled dry and needs to be used again. Please follow these instructions carefully to ensure the device remains safe for operation. 

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked if you can take the battery apart to investigate a burning smell from your Mira vacuum. Our help article "Burning smell from your Mira robot vacuum" says you must not dismantle the battery.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your Fenwick cooker hood and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about the error code E-8525 and the burning smell coming from your appliance. Our help article "Burning smell from your Fenwick cooker hood" says the code E-8525 indicates that the fan motor on your cooker hood has overheated. This overheating can be the cause of the burning smell that you have noticed from your unit.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. If the plug and surrounding area are wet, you should isolate the power at the fuse box instead of unplugging the appliance. You are concerned about the safest way to turn off your Vale fridge when water is present near the electrics. Our help article "Water leaking underneath your Vale fridge freezer" provides these instructions for this situation.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your cooker and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about the expected arrival time for an engineer if you are an Extended Care member and report a safety concern. Our Safety and recalls policy, section "Extended Care: Safety checks under the plan", says as an Extended Care member, you will get an engineer within 7 hours of reporting a safety concern to us.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You asked if you can continue using your Ashby dryer while the mesh on your filter is torn. Our help article "Replacing a damaged lint filter" says you must stop using the dryer until the damaged filter has been replaced to prevent lint from passing into the airflow system.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking if it is appropriate to use a 30°C setting for your regular laundry when the labels permit it. Our help article "Saving energy with your Keel washing machine" says you should choose a 30°C wash for lightly soiled everyday clothes, provided their care labels allow it. Using lower wash temperatures reduces the energy needed to heat the water.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked for the reference number for the compressor start relay in your Vale fridge, which has a burning smell. Our help article "Burning smell from your Vale fridge freezer" says the compressor start relay reference number is KX-2645. This information relates to your request regarding the specific part number for your appliance. 

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using your appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked if you may take your Mira vacuum casing apart to clear out debris after it has cooled down. Our help article "Burning smell from your Mira robot vacuum" says you must not dismantle the vacuum. You should only remove loose material you can reach without opening the casing.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the requirements for packing your Mira robot vacuum for a return when the original box is not available. Our Returns and refunds policy, section "Mira robot vacuum: Packaging and condition", says you should use a strong box with suitable cushioning to ensure the appliance sits securely without moving or pressing against the sides. You must avoid using loose packing materials that could enter openings or become caught in moving parts. Please contact Halvard Home if you are unsure whether your packaging is suitable.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked if you must pay if you choose not to proceed with an oven repair after an engineer has visited. Our Servicing and engineer visits policy, section "Charges", says an attendance or assessment charge may apply even if you decide not to proceed with a repair. We inform you of this charge at the time of booking.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about a burning smell coming from your Fenwick hood and how long to leave it switched off. Our help article "Burning smell from your Fenwick cooker hood" says do not restart the hood to check if the smell has cleared. Keep it switched off until a qualified service engineer has inspected it.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked how long you need to wait after emptying your Brio kettle before you can safely check the filter due to an E-2393 error. Our help article "Replacing the Brio kettle’s filter" says you must leave the kettle to cool for 15 minutes before checking the filter.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about a burning smell coming from the back of your Vale fridge freezer and how long to wait before restarting it. Our help article "Burning smell from your Vale fridge freezer" says you should not restart the fridge freezer to check whether the smell has gone. Please stop using the appliance immediately and contact Halvard Home support to arrange an inspection.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You asked how to safely turn off your Corra hob due to a rattling sound and error code E-9865. Our help article "Unusual vibration from your Corra induction hob" says you should stop cooking and switch the hob off using its controls. Once the cooling fan has stopped, turn off the hob’s electricity supply at the wall isolator and leave it switched off until it has been checked.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You have asked about the safety steps for cleaning a Keel washing machine filter when the machine is draining slowly. Our help article "Cleaning your Keel washing machine filter" says you should switch off and unplug the machine first. If you have recently used a hot wash, you must let the water cool completely before you begin.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}
